# =====================================================================
# Release V170 -- carry the associate pay % onto Gold.Dim_Practitioners
# =====================================================================
# Adds Associate_Pct (whole percent, as entered on the app's Finance settings page) to the
# practitioner dimension, so the model can split revenue per practitioner.
#
# WHY HERE AND NOT A NEW TABLE. The rate already exists in Input.Practitioner_Pay, and
# Gold.Aggregate_Practitioner_Contribution already applies it -- but only to PRODUCTION
# (SUM(Fact_Invoice_Items.Total_Price)), which is invoice-priced and therefore EXCLUDES NHS/UDA
# income and plan capitation. The new Earnings/Contribution measures are wanted on Total Revenue,
# which includes both. Rather than rebuild that aggregate on a wider base, the rate rides on the
# dimension that the revenue fact ALREADY joins to -- so there is no new relationship to wire into
# the semantic model, and the split can be evaluated per practitioner in DAX over any revenue base.
#
# NULL IS NOT ZERO. A practitioner with no rate recorded -- a principal, typically -- is left NULL
# and keeps the whole of their revenue. That is the same assumption
# Gold.Aggregate_Practitioner_Contribution already makes, and writing 0 instead would mean the same
# thing here but the opposite thing if the column were ever read as "their share".
#
# ==> FIVE PLACES, AND MISSING ONE IS SILENT. <== The load is a hash-gated MERGE:
#   * the #src SELECT        -- where the value comes from (Practitioner_PAY; note FTE beside it
#                               comes from Practitioner_ROLE, and both Input tables carry an FTE
#                               column, which is an easy mis-read)
#   * the UPDATE SET list    -- or an edited rate never reaches an existing practitioner
#   * BOTH sides of the hash -- omit either and a rate change hashes identical, so the MERGE skips
#                               the row: the rate would update for new practitioners only, and
#                               changing an existing one would appear to do nothing
#   * the INSERT column list -- or a newly-arrived practitioner lands with a NULL rate
#
# The PBI view is regenerated so 'List Practitioners' exposes the column; the semantic model still
# needs the table refreshed in Power BI Desktop before the column appears there.
#
# Guarded ALTER, so idempotent and safe to re-run.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V170__associate_pct_on_dim_practitioners.manifest
# =====================================================================

# The column is added by a GUARDED ALTER, NOT by deploying Gold.Dim_Practitioners.Table.sql.
# That file opens with DROP TABLE IF EXISTS -- it is the canonical full-rebuild script. Dropping
# this dimension would reassign every pk_Practitioner (the load numbers them from
# MAX(pk)+ROW_NUMBER()), and the facts that reference them are HASH-GATED: unchanged fact rows are
# skipped on reload, so their fk_Practitioner would keep pointing at surrogate keys that now mean a
# different person. Silent, and wrong in the reports rather than in an error. The canonical file
# carries the column too, so a genuine full rebuild includes it.
EXEC     IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA='Gold' AND TABLE_NAME='Dim_Practitioners' AND COLUMN_NAME='Associate_Pct') ALTER TABLE [Gold].[Dim_Practitioners] ADD [Associate_Pct] [decimal](6,3) NULL;

DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Dim_Practitioners.StoredProcedure.sql
# Gold.vw_Dim_Practitioners OVERRIDES the table: Meta.usp_Create_Gold_Views skips a Gold table
# whenever a vw_<table> exists, so PBI.[List Practitioners] is generated from this view's
# explicit column list. Adding the column to the TABLE alone leaves the model unable to see it
# -- which is exactly what happened on the first run of this release.
DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.vw_Dim_Practitioners.View.sql

EXEC     DECLARE @i BIGINT,@u BIGINT,@d BIGINT; EXEC Gold.usp_Load_Dim_Practitioners @Mode='PROD',@Run_Inserts=@i OUT,@Run_Updates=@u OUT,@Run_Deletes=@d OUT;
EXEC     EXEC Meta.usp_Create_Gold_Views;

TEST
